      "seed": 2055729779,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1236387917,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781010879884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Decoration markers (v9 · round-3)\n\n@intent <path> [<clause-ids>]\n    declarations OR non-declaration statements\n    focal claim — 'this is what makes\n    the clause hold'\n\n@intent-support <path> [<clause-ids>]\n                [<subj>, <pred>, <obj>]\n    non-declaration statements only\n    inline NL triple describes statement role\n    SLOTS ARE ALWAYS AFFIRMATIVE\n\n@intent-test <path>/<configured-suffix>\n    test declarations\n\n@intent-test-file <path>/<configured-suffix>\n    file-scope test claim · top of file\n\n@intent-file / @intent-ignore  (unchanged)\n\n— Polarity (NEW v9 round-3) —\nTriples carry polarity: positive | negative\n(default positive). Slots stay affirmative.\nRuntime inverts the LLM verdict post-call.\nThe LLM NEVER sees a negated question.\n\n— Negation parser rule (§3.1.1) —\nMatrix-predicate negation REJECTED in\npredicate slot (lexicon: not, never,\nfails to, lacks, excludes, omits, forbids,\nprohibits, prevents, denies, devoid of, …).\nConstituent negation inside noun phrases\n('a function with no required arguments')\nis LEGAL in subject/object slots.\n\n— Quantifier (NEW v9) —\nquantifier: at-least-one (default) | each |\nexactly-one | at-most-one | none |\nat-least-N | at-most-N · with optional scope:.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "card-decorators",
      "originalText": "Decoration markers (v9 · round-3)\n\n@intent <path> [<clause-ids>]\n    declarations OR non-declaration statements\n    focal claim — 'this is what makes\n    the clause hold'\n\n@intent-support <path> [<clause-ids>]\n                [<subj>, <pred>, <obj>]\n    non-declaration statements only\n    inline NL triple describes statement role\n    SLOTS ARE ALWAYS AFFIRMATIVE\n\n@intent-test <path>/<configured-suffix>\n    test declarations\n\n@intent-test-file <path>/<configured-suffix>\n    file-scope test claim · top of file\n\n@intent-file / @intent-ignore  (unchanged)\n\n— Polarity (NEW v9 round-3) —\nTriples carry polarity: positive | negative\n(default positive). Slots stay affirmative.\nRuntime inverts the LLM verdict post-call.\nThe LLM NEVER sees a negated question.\n\n— Negation parser rule (§3.1.1) —\nMatrix-predicate negation REJECTED in\npredicate slot (lexicon: not, never,\nfails to, lacks, excludes, omits, forbids,\nprohibits, prevents, denies, devoid of, …).\nConstituent negation inside noun phrases\n('a function with no required arguments')\nis LEGAL in subject/object slots.\n\n— Quantifier (NEW v9) —\nquantifier: at-least-one (default) | each |\nexactly-one | at-most-one | none |\nat-least-N | at-most-N · with optional scope:.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "Jyyp6YQvg94fUDXEPq5m8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2826.2109375,
      "y": 7866.2109375,
      "width": 262.705078125,
      "height": 524.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1F2E4D",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1818700819,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1311496461,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781010879884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "PreToolUse gate — 10 mechanical checks\n(no LLM · no semantic analysis)\n\n  1. Decorator present on every exported decl\n  2. Every intent path resolves\n  3. Every aspect/clause id resolves to a triple\n  4. One intent per line\n  5. @intent-ignore has both because=(...)\n      and reason=\"...\"\n  6. Every statement inside a decorated   (v9)\n      declaration is decorated\n  7. @intent-support has a valid           (v9)\n      3-slot triple\n  8. No statement carries both @intent     (v9)\n      and @intent-support for the same intent\n  9. @intent-test/-test-file path ends in  (v9)\n      any configured test_pyramid.suffix\n 10. No matrix-predicate negation in     (round-3)\n      @intent-support's predicate slot —\n      author must use polarity: negative instead\n\nDecorate-or-decompose (S ⊆ D) is NOT in the\ngate (agentic). REPROMOTED to Sprint 9 as\n/dusk-doctor --static-analysis for drift\ndetection — runs off the write path.\n\n— dusk init merge strategy (round-3) —\nWrites hook with _dusk_marker: 'dusk-pre-tool-\nuse-gate' + _dusk_managed: 'v1' as idempotency\nanchor. On conflict with existing non-Dusk\nPreToolUse entry matching Write/Edit: prompts\nuser [1] append (recommended), [2] replace\n(writes .claude/settings.json.bak), [3] abort.\nNever silent clobber. dusk doctor --check-hook\n[--repair] verifies installation.\n\nGate is HARD: failed check → write rejected →\nEngineer re-drafts. No 'warning' mode.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "card-pretooluse",
      "originalText": "PreToolUse gate — 10 mechanical checks\n(no LLM · no semantic analysis)\n\n  1. Decorator present on every exported decl\n  2. Every intent path resolves\n  3. Every aspect/clause id resolves to a triple\n  4. One intent per line\n  5. @intent-ignore has both because=(...)\n      and reason=\"...\"\n  6. Every statement inside a decorated   (v9)\n      declaration is decorated\n  7. @intent-support has a valid           (v9)\n      3-slot triple\n  8. No statement carries both @intent     (v9)\n      and @intent-support for the same intent\n  9. @intent-test/-test-file path ends in  (v9)\n      any configured test_pyramid.suffix\n 10. No matrix-predicate negation in     (round-3)\n      @intent-support's predicate slot —\n      author must use polarity: negative instead\n\nDecorate-or-decompose (S ⊆ D) is NOT in the\ngate (agentic). REPROMOTED to Sprint 9 as\n/dusk-doctor --static-analysis for drift\ndetection — runs off the write path.\n\n— dusk init merge strategy (round-3) —\nWrites hook with _dusk_marker: 'dusk-pre-tool-\nuse-gate' + _dusk_managed: 'v1' as idempotency\nanchor. On conflict with existing non-Dusk\nPreToolUse entry matching Write/Edit: prompts\nuser [1] append (recommended), [2] replace\n(writes .claude/settings.json.bak), [3] abort.\nNever silent clobber. dusk doctor --check-hook\n[--repair] verifies installation.\n\nGate is HARD: failed check → write rejected →\nEngineer re-drafts. No 'warning' mode.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "2HkiEmnTZ2-14WEs1Z4yY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5566.2109375,
      "y": 7866.2109375,
      "width": 333.802734375,
      "height": 468.04999999999995,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1F2E4D",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2104373683,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 2053683661,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781010879884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Decoration-completeness mandate (DESIGN)\n\nEvery line, call, assignment, statement,\nexpression, and lambda body — and their\ncontents — must be covered by intent\ndecorators appropriate to their participation.\n\nWhen a code unit's contents include\noperations whose intent participation\ndiffers from the unit's decoration, the\nunit is DECOMPOSED so each sub-operation\ncan be decorated appropriately.\n\nv1 enforcement (round-3):\n  · Engineer proactively applies the mandate\n    (role prompt + decoration-completeness skill)\n  · Verifier surfaces unsatisfied aspects when\n    sub-operations participate in undeclared intents\n  · /dusk-doctor --static-analysis (REPROMOTED to v1, Sprint 9)\n    runs S⊆D call-graph check off the write path — drift detection,\n    not real-time enforcement. Conservative default; --strict-unknowns\n    surfaces undecorated callees.\n  · NOT in the PreToolUse gate (agentic)\n\nExamples\n  pubsub.publish(syncChannel(\"n\"), event)\n    → channel-resolution intent ≠ publish\n      intent → EXTRACT syncChannel call\n\n  db.insert(x).values(y).returning()\n    → all steps share intent footprint\n      → keep as one statement\n\nLanguage-agnostic: the rule speaks about\nintent participation, not syntactic shape.\nTypeScript, Python, Go, Rust, SQL — same\nrule.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "card-codestyle",
      "originalText": "Decoration-completeness mandate (DESIGN)\n\nEvery line, call, assignment, statement,\nexpression, and lambda body — and their\ncontents — must be covered by intent\ndecorators appropriate to their participation.\n\nWhen a code unit's contents include\noperations whose intent participation\ndiffers from the unit's decoration, the\nunit is DECOMPOSED so each sub-operation\ncan be decorated appropriately.\n\nv1 enforcement (round-3):\n  · Engineer proactively applies the mandate\n    (role prompt + decoration-completeness skill)\n  · Verifier surfaces unsatisfied aspects when\n    sub-operations participate in undeclared intents\n  · /dusk-doctor --static-analysis (REPROMOTED to v1, Sprint 9)\n    runs S⊆D call-graph check off the write path — drift detection,\n    not real-time enforcement. Conservative default; --strict-unknowns\n    surfaces undecorated callees.\n  · NOT in the PreToolUse gate (agentic)\n\nExamples\n  pubsub.publish(syncChannel(\"n\"), event)\n    → channel-resolution intent ≠ publish\n      intent → EXTRACT syncChannel call\n\n  db.insert(x).values(y).returning()\n    → all steps share intent footprint\n      → keep as one statement\n\nLanguage-agnostic: the rule speaks about\nintent participation, not syntactic shape.\nTypeScript, Python, Go, Rust, SQL — same\nrule.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "cTQWBStL2IBiR4WxpKMQ8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8306.2109375,
      "y": 7866.2109375,
      "width": 412.541015625,
      "height": 455.4,
      "angle": 0,
