      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Integration surface — MCP + slash (round-3)\n\nMCP tools (mutating + flow):\n  dusk_implement({request? | resume_token?})   pipeline OR resume\n  dusk_author_start({request})         → dialog_id + first question\n  dusk_author_continue({dialog_id, response})  loop until finalized\n  dusk_author_finalize({dialog_id})    → intents_created\n  dusk_resolve_livelock({bead_id, verb})  accept_test_as_is\n                                          | modify_triple | escalate\n  dusk_cancel({bead_id?, reason})  → CancelResult (cooperative)\n  dusk_verify({diff, intents?})    → Verdict (ad-hoc)\n\nRead-only fallback tools (paired with MCP resources):\n  dusk_list_intents / dusk_get_intent\n  dusk_list_traces / dusk_list_beads / dusk_get_bead\n  dusk_list_implement_checkpoints · dusk_status · dusk_inspect\n\nMCP resources (preferred when host browses):\n  dusk://intents · dusk://intents/<path> · dusk://traces/recent\n  dusk://beads/active · dusk://beads/<id> · dusk://implement-checkpoints\n\nSlash commands (user-facing):\n  /dusk-init · /dusk-author · /dusk-status · /dusk-verify\n  /dusk-test · /dusk-benchmark · /dusk-doctor\n  /dusk-doctor --static-analysis (S⊆D drift detection)\n  /dusk-doctor --check-hook [--repair]\n\nHarness contract — 4 capabilities (round-3, reduced from 5):\n  spawn-by-type (Task tool) · PreToolUse hook (per-session)\n  MCP host · filesystem trace emission\n  (Skill scoping is Dusk-owned, not harness-provided.)\n\nEvery MCP tool returns success OR DuskError {kind, recoverable,\nrecovery_hint, …}. Pause/resume + cancellation are FIRST-CLASS\nsemantics, not afterthoughts.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "card-mcp",
      "originalText": "Integration surface — MCP + slash (round-3)\n\nMCP tools (mutating + flow):\n  dusk_implement({request? | resume_token?})   pipeline OR resume\n  dusk_author_start({request})         → dialog_id + first question\n  dusk_author_continue({dialog_id, response})  loop until finalized\n  dusk_author_finalize({dialog_id})    → intents_created\n  dusk_resolve_livelock({bead_id, verb})  accept_test_as_is\n                                          | modify_triple | escalate\n  dusk_cancel({bead_id?, reason})  → CancelResult (cooperative)\n  dusk_verify({diff, intents?})    → Verdict (ad-hoc)\n\nRead-only fallback tools (paired with MCP resources):\n  dusk_list_intents / dusk_get_intent\n  dusk_list_traces / dusk_list_beads / dusk_get_bead\n  dusk_list_implement_checkpoints · dusk_status · dusk_inspect\n\nMCP resources (preferred when host browses):\n  dusk://intents · dusk://intents/<path> · dusk://traces/recent\n  dusk://beads/active · dusk://beads/<id> · dusk://implement-checkpoints\n\nSlash commands (user-facing):\n  /dusk-init · /dusk-author · /dusk-status · /dusk-verify\n  /dusk-test · /dusk-benchmark · /dusk-doctor\n  /dusk-doctor --static-analysis (S⊆D drift detection)\n  /dusk-doctor --check-hook [--repair]\n\nHarness contract — 4 capabilities (round-3, reduced from 5):\n  spawn-by-type (Task tool) · PreToolUse hook (per-session)\n  MCP host · filesystem trace emission\n  (Skill scoping is Dusk-owned, not harness-provided.)\n\nEvery MCP tool returns success OR DuskError {kind, recoverable,\nrecovery_hint, …}. Pause/resume + cancellation are FIRST-CLASS\nsemantics, not afterthoughts.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
