      "updated": 1781010879884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Test pyramid encoding (v9 · round-3)\n\nReserved child-intent suffixes (CONFIGURABLE via\ndusk.config.yml > test_pyramid.suffixes — defaults below):\n  <impl-intent>/unit-tests          pure · no DB · no network\n  <impl-intent>/integration-tests   cross-component · real DB\n  <impl-intent>/e2e-tests           full journey · real HTTP + DB\n  (extensible: contract-tests, property-tests, fuzz-tests, …)\n\nTest intent triples (affirmative + polarity per round-3):\n  covers-X        'the suite include a passing case verifying …'\n  isolated-from-Y polarity: negative on 'depends on Y'\n  count-bounds    quantifier: exactly-one + scope: per inserted row\n\nTwo-stage satisfaction (NEW v9 — round-3):\n  1. Verifier evaluates the test BODY against the test-intent\n     triples (does the test body actually verify what the triple\n     claims?). A trivially-passing test FAILS this check.\n  2. Test Runner executes only Verifier-validated tests.\n\nLivelock detection (round-3):\n  Same triple ≥3 iters + slot-focus ≥80% concentration +\n  ≥3 structural test approaches (mock-call-order, time-spy,\n  state-observation, snapshot-of-events, instrumented-mock, …)\n  → TestVerifierLivelockReport → user resolves via\n  dusk_resolve_livelock(accept_test_as_is | modify_triple |\n  escalate).\n\nHierarchical satisfaction: parent X satisfied iff\n  (X's triples pass via two-verdict {focal+support}) AND\n  (every test-child satisfies BOTH stages).",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "card-testpyramid",
      "originalText": "Test pyramid encoding (v9 · round-3)\n\nReserved child-intent suffixes (CONFIGURABLE via\ndusk.config.yml > test_pyramid.suffixes — defaults below):\n  <impl-intent>/unit-tests          pure · no DB · no network\n  <impl-intent>/integration-tests   cross-component · real DB\n  <impl-intent>/e2e-tests           full journey · real HTTP + DB\n  (extensible: contract-tests, property-tests, fuzz-tests, …)\n\nTest intent triples (affirmative + polarity per round-3):\n  covers-X        'the suite include a passing case verifying …'\n  isolated-from-Y polarity: negative on 'depends on Y'\n  count-bounds    quantifier: exactly-one + scope: per inserted row\n\nTwo-stage satisfaction (NEW v9 — round-3):\n  1. Verifier evaluates the test BODY against the test-intent\n     triples (does the test body actually verify what the triple\n     claims?). A trivially-passing test FAILS this check.\n  2. Test Runner executes only Verifier-validated tests.\n\nLivelock detection (round-3):\n  Same triple ≥3 iters + slot-focus ≥80% concentration +\n  ≥3 structural test approaches (mock-call-order, time-spy,\n  state-observation, snapshot-of-events, instrumented-mock, …)\n  → TestVerifierLivelockReport → user resolves via\n  dusk_resolve_livelock(accept_test_as_is | modify_triple |\n  escalate).\n\nHierarchical satisfaction: parent X satisfied iff\n  (X's triples pass via two-verdict {focal+support}) AND\n  (every test-child satisfies BOTH stages).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
