      "updated": 1781010879884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What's new in v9 round-3 (key hardenings)\n\nConstraint language\n  · Polarity field replaces affirmative-only-by-rewriting.\n    Slots stay affirmative; runtime inverts post-LLM.\n    LLM NEVER sees negation. Matrix/constituent parser rule.\n  · compose: implies with CLOSED antecedent vocabulary\n    (is decorated with · claims any aspect of · is enclosed by\n    a decoration of). Antecedents evaluated by deterministic\n    INDEX LOOKUP, never LLM-judged.\n  · quantifier vocab on triples + optional scope:.\n  · Typed relates_to (5 kinds: parent · implies · conflicts ·\n    supersedes · sibling). refines collapsed into parent.\n  · Schema version 2 · automatic v8 migration.\n\nPipeline & runtime\n  · Session-snapshot index (immutable for run) + per-bead\n    in-memory delta. Reads carry index_snapshot_id.\n  · Stuckness detector early-fires diagnosis; iter-5 fallback.\n  · Diagnosis to BEAD ORCHESTRATOR only — Verifier spawn\n    payload is identical across iterations (asymmetry protected).\n  · 40-iter bead lifetime budget + 4-level recovery ladder\n    (partial commit → intent-modification proposal → freeze → abort).\n  · Long cycle: N=10 + N=2 confirmation pass on first reject\n    (filters Verifier variance).\n  · File-overlap + cross-bead focal/support overlap in DAG.\n\nVerification\n  · Per-triple verdict split: focal_verdict + support_quality.\n  · Per-support-claim verdict (matches | mismatch | vague).\n  · Fresh-Verifier audit: 3 axes (variance + similarity +\n    CITATION PRECISION). No LLM-judge in the audit itself.\n  · Two-stage test satisfaction: Verifier validates test body\n    BEFORE Test Runner executes.\n  · TestVerifierLivelockReport + dusk_resolve_livelock.\n\nIntegration surface\n  · Harness contract: 4 capabilities (was 5). Tool/skill scoping\n    is ADVISORY in v1; PreToolUse gate provides safety.\n  · Sub-agent spawn via Claude Code Task tool.\n  · dusk_implement pause/resume via disk checkpoint + resume_token\n    (DuskError{kind: implement_paused_for_authoring}).\n  · dusk_author_* continuation pattern (start/continue/finalize).\n  · dusk_cancel: cooperative — drains in-flight Task calls,\n    ordered cleanup, distinguishes cancelled[] from preserved[].\n  · dusk_resolve_livelock + paired list/get tools + MCP resources.\n  · DuskError envelope on every MCP tool.\n  · dusk init writes hook with _dusk_marker idempotency anchor +\n    conflict-prompting three-option merge. Never silent clobber.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "card-whatsnew",
      "originalText": "What's new in v9 round-3 (key hardenings)\n\nConstraint language\n  · Polarity field replaces affirmative-only-by-rewriting.\n    Slots stay affirmative; runtime inverts post-LLM.\n    LLM NEVER sees negation. Matrix/constituent parser rule.\n  · compose: implies with CLOSED antecedent vocabulary\n    (is decorated with · claims any aspect of · is enclosed by\n    a decoration of). Antecedents evaluated by deterministic\n    INDEX LOOKUP, never LLM-judged.\n  · quantifier vocab on triples + optional scope:.\n  · Typed relates_to (5 kinds: parent · implies · conflicts ·\n    supersedes · sibling). refines collapsed into parent.\n  · Schema version 2 · automatic v8 migration.\n\nPipeline & runtime\n  · Session-snapshot index (immutable for run) + per-bead\n    in-memory delta. Reads carry index_snapshot_id.\n  · Stuckness detector early-fires diagnosis; iter-5 fallback.\n  · Diagnosis to BEAD ORCHESTRATOR only — Verifier spawn\n    payload is identical across iterations (asymmetry protected).\n  · 40-iter bead lifetime budget + 4-level recovery ladder\n    (partial commit → intent-modification proposal → freeze → abort).\n  · Long cycle: N=10 + N=2 confirmation pass on first reject\n    (filters Verifier variance).\n  · File-overlap + cross-bead focal/support overlap in DAG.\n\nVerification\n  · Per-triple verdict split: focal_verdict + support_quality.\n  · Per-support-claim verdict (matches | mismatch | vague).\n  · Fresh-Verifier audit: 3 axes (variance + similarity +\n    CITATION PRECISION). No LLM-judge in the audit itself.\n  · Two-stage test satisfaction: Verifier validates test body\n    BEFORE Test Runner executes.\n  · TestVerifierLivelockReport + dusk_resolve_livelock.\n\nIntegration surface\n  · Harness contract: 4 capabilities (was 5). Tool/skill scoping\n    is ADVISORY in v1; PreToolUse gate provides safety.\n  · Sub-agent spawn via Claude Code Task tool.\n  · dusk_implement pause/resume via disk checkpoint + resume_token\n    (DuskError{kind: implement_paused_for_authoring}).\n  · dusk_author_* continuation pattern (start/continue/finalize).\n  · dusk_cancel: cooperative — drains in-flight Task calls,\n    ordered cleanup, distinguishes cancelled[] from preserved[].\n  · dusk_resolve_livelock + paired list/get tools + MCP resources.\n  · DuskError envelope on every MCP tool.\n  · dusk init writes hook with _dusk_marker idempotency anchor +\n    conflict-prompting three-option merge. Never silent clobber.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "VO0tUKt9oFV3yRa4DWY2P",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 86.2109375,
      "y": 10626.2109375,
      "width": 280.6396484375,
      "height": 379.49999999999994,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1F2E4D",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 246091443,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1325871245,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781010879884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reading the example\n\nThe function declaration claims FIVE intents:\n  notifications/send (primary, with aspects)\n  db/use-drizzle-orm (cross-cutting · touched)\n  sync/pubsub-on-create (cross-cutting · touched)\n  observability/structured-logging (cross-cutting)\n  error-handling/observable-failures (cross-cutting)\n\nInside the body, every statement is decorated:\n  @intent          when the statement IS the focal\n                       achievement of an aspect\n  @intent-support  when the statement contributes\n                       (with NL triple describing role)\n\nKey structural moves (Engineer's discipline):\n  · syncChannel(\"notification\") extracted ABOVE the loop\n      (loop-invariant hoist · check 8)\n  · the event object extracted from the publish call args\n      (no nested user fn call · check 8)\n  · inArray(...) predicates extracted before Drizzle chains\n  · Date.now() extracted to a named const\n  · getLogger() extracted; payload object extracted;\n      then logger.info(payload, msg)\n  · let sent/skipped/failed collapsed to one counters obj\n  · else-if chain flattened with continue\n\nVerifier reads SCOPED — per aspect, not whole function:\n  for publish-sync-per-insert it reads ~4 lines\n  (focal + 3 support claims), not the 90-line body.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "code-callout",
      "originalText": "Reading the example\n\nThe function declaration claims FIVE intents:\n  notifications/send (primary, with aspects)\n  db/use-drizzle-orm (cross-cutting · touched)\n  sync/pubsub-on-create (cross-cutting · touched)\n  observability/structured-logging (cross-cutting)\n  error-handling/observable-failures (cross-cutting)\n\nInside the body, every statement is decorated:\n  @intent          when the statement IS the focal\n                       achievement of an aspect\n  @intent-support  when the statement contributes\n                       (with NL triple describing role)\n\nKey structural moves (Engineer's discipline):\n  · syncChannel(\"notification\") extracted ABOVE the loop\n      (loop-invariant hoist · check 8)\n  · the event object extracted from the publish call args\n      (no nested user fn call · check 8)\n  · inArray(...) predicates extracted before Drizzle chains\n  · Date.now() extracted to a named const\n  · getLogger() extracted; payload object extracted;\n      then logger.info(payload, msg)\n  · let sent/skipped/failed collapsed to one counters obj\n  · else-if chain flattened with continue\n\nVerifier reads SCOPED — per aspect, not whole function:\n  for publish-sync-per-insert it reads ~4 lines\n  (focal + 3 support claims), not the 90-line body.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
